  "notes": "Body: 12 segments, 9 profile points = 168 triangles.  O 0.0900 outer, 0.1000 tall; wall 4.4 mm at the rim, floor 9 mm, flat rim annulus, outer wall split at z=0.0940 for the glaze band.  Handle: 6-sided tube, 11 stations, 4.5 mm necked roots against a 5.2 mm section, 132 triangles, both caps buried in the wall at x=0.0415 between the inner (0.0402) and outer (0.0450) surfaces, so nothing enters the cavity; apex ring still reaches x=0.0752, keeping the pre-scale AABB at 0.1202 x 0.0900 x 0.1000.  About 330 triangles after the Exact union.  Four slots by face position: red glaze above z=0.0935 on the outside plus the rim annulus, ceramic_dark inside (r<0.0435) and on the foot (z<0.0045), ink within 7.5 mm of the two handle roots, ceramic elsewhere.  One closed shell.",
